1306
00:43:30,267 --> 00:43:30,867
Get away.

1307
00:43:36,933 --> 00:43:38,433
-Oh, 15 minute break, everybody.

1308
00:43:38,467 --> 00:43:39,967
Lippert rules apply here.

1309
00:43:45,333 --> 00:43:47,867
-I love these-- birds.

1310
00:43:47,900 --> 00:43:51,033
-Ah, thank you, Captain Cutaway.

1311
00:43:51,067 --> 00:43:52,900
-What time would you say it is?

1312
00:43:52,933 --> 00:43:53,867
-Oh, it's time to
kill something.

1313
00:43:56,900 --> 00:43:58,300
-I'd say it's about 3
o'clock Earth time here.

1314
00:43:58,333 --> 00:43:59,267
-Judging by those birds.

1315
00:43:59,300 --> 00:44:01,133
-Except we don't know
how many hours there

1316
00:44:01,167 --> 00:44:02,400
are in the daily cycle here.

1317
00:44:02,433 --> 00:44:05,033
Yo know, this place could move
around faster than our Earth.

1318
00:44:05,067 --> 00:44:06,967
-Well, let's figure
for 3 o'clock anyway.

1319
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:08,867
That gives us three or
four hours before dark.

1320
00:44:08,900 --> 00:44:11,433
-Besides, I decided I'm
the new god of this planet.

1321
00:44:18,933 --> 00:44:20,533
[Mock shock]

1322
00:44:20,567 --> 00:44:22,933
-Dick, that outcropping's
further than we thought.

1323
00:44:22,967 --> 00:44:25,867
-Ah, a couple more miles
should bring us there.

1324
00:44:25,900 --> 00:44:27,367
-A couple more miles
as the crow flies,

1325
00:44:27,400 --> 00:44:29,333
but five miles up
and down those hills.

1326
00:44:29,367 --> 00:44:31,200
-I symbolically represent
the pace of this film.

1327
00:44:34,567 --> 00:44:36,067
-Hm, we're making
pretty good time,

1328
00:44:36,100 --> 00:44:38,833
considering this
is a Lippert film.

1329
00:44:38,867 --> 00:44:40,167
[Animal noises]

1330
00:44:47,533 --> 00:44:52,900
-Lions and tigers
and bears-- oh, my!

1331
00:44:52,933 --> 00:44:55,100
-And there on the handle was
some stock footage of a hook.

1332
00:44:55,133 --> 00:44:58,300
-What do you think, Nora?

1333
00:44:58,333 --> 00:45:01,033
-About the age of this place?

1334
00:45:01,067 --> 00:45:02,500
I'm afraid your guess was right.

1335
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:05,567
It's pretty young as planets
go, much younger than our Earth.

1336
00:45:05,600 --> 00:45:08,400
-Uh, could you be a
little more vague, Nora?

1337
00:45:08,433 --> 00:45:10,333
-Prehistoric.

1338
00:45:10,367 --> 00:45:13,433
-Are you serious, Nora?

1339
00:45:13,467 --> 00:45:16,200
Look, let's get out of here
and get back to the ship.

1340
00:45:16,233 --> 00:45:18,100
I'm scared to death, and
I don't mind admitting it.

1341
00:45:18,133 --> 00:45:21,033
-Oh, thank you, Mrs.
Dedicated Scientist.

1342
00:45:21,033 --> 00:45:24,567
-Yes, for the kind of
preliminary survey they want.

1343
00:45:24,600 --> 00:45:27,200
