quick visit before we leave.

1352
00:45:41,067 --> 00:45:41,433
-Mm-hmm.

1353
00:45:41,467 --> 00:45:42,267
May be fun.

1354
00:45:42,300 --> 00:45:44,467
-Let the next people
pay it a visit.

1355
00:45:44,500 --> 00:45:46,567
Let's get back to the
ship, get out of here,

1356
00:45:46,600 --> 00:45:48,133
before something awful happens--

1357
00:45:48,167 --> 00:45:49,167
-Let's all get out of here.

1358
00:45:49,200 --> 00:45:50,467
-Yeah.

1359
00:45:50,500 --> 00:45:52,667
Wouldn't want them to find an
important scientific discovery.

1360
00:45:52,700 --> 00:45:54,933
-If it doesn't get dark
too soon, we're all right.

1361
00:46:05,233 --> 00:46:06,100
-Hey, you guys.

1362
00:46:06,133 --> 00:46:07,267
I got this puppet.

1363
00:46:07,300 --> 00:46:10,100
Let's do that little song
and sketch about the lemur.

1364
00:46:10,133 --> 00:46:10,500
-All right.

1365
00:46:10,533 --> 00:46:11,633
-Cue it.

1366
00:46:11,667 --> 00:46:14,033
-(SINGING) It's Joey the
lemur, the friend to mankind.

1367
00:46:14,067 --> 00:46:16,000
Our furry sort of monkey
friend, he really does shine.

1368
00:46:16,033 --> 00:46:17,033
Hey.

1369
00:46:17,067 --> 00:46:19,000
-Joey, the lemur is
really fun to have around.

1370
00:46:19,033 --> 00:46:22,200
He'll huggle and dart
you, fun, fun, fun.

1371
00:46:22,233 --> 00:46:23,067
-Joey, the lemur.

1372
00:46:23,100 --> 00:46:24,300
He'll run everywhere.

1373
00:46:24,333 --> 00:46:27,633
Joey the lemur, what kind of
heck of animal is he, anyway?

1374
00:46:27,667 --> 00:46:29,800
Um, Joey, the lemur,
the kind of animal

1375
00:46:29,833 --> 00:46:31,433
that would go to the
bathroom anywhere.

1376
00:46:31,467 --> 00:46:32,300
-Hold it.

1377
00:46:32,333 --> 00:46:33,500
Just hold it.

1378
00:46:33,533 --> 00:46:35,200
-But there's more.

1379
00:46:35,233 --> 00:46:36,400
-That's OK.

1380
00:46:36,433 --> 00:46:40,200
This is the lemur, native to
Philippines and Madagascar.

1381
00:46:40,233 --> 00:46:44,400
Uh-- uh, and fictional
planets like Nova.

1382
00:46:44,433 --> 00:46:48,767
Um, he is a clean,
gregarious, and good pet.

1383
00:46:48,800 --> 00:46:50,367
You said it, pal.

1384
00:46:50,400 --> 00:46:53,500
Old boy, pal of mine,
you're the one for me.

1385
00:46:53,533 --> 00:46:56,333
-Uh-oh, Joel's swinging
into his puppet routine.

1386
00:46:56,367 --> 00:46:58,267
-Hey, can it, fire plug.

1387
00:46:58,300 --> 00:46:58,933
-Hey.

1388
00:46:58,967 --> 00:47:00,667
-I've had enough out of you.

1389
00:47:00,733 --> 00:47:01,633
-Joey, the lemur--

1390
00:47:01,633 --> 00:47:02,900
-I got a story to tell.

1391
00:47:02,933 --> 00:47:03,933
--he'll say what he thinks.

1392
00:47:03,967 --> 00:47:04,833
-Oh, boy.

1393
00:47:04,867 --> 00:47:05,733
Will I ever?

1394
00:47:05,767 --> 00:47:07,633
I'll carry on like
a Gilbert Gottfried

1395
00:47:07,667 --> 00:47:10,233
from the animal world, I
don't mind telling you.

1396
00:47:10,267 --> 00:47:13,333
You know, I'm the clown prince
of the primate world, who's

1397
00:47:13,367 --> 00:47:17,667
often-- who's often mistaken
for our friend, the chimpanzee.

1398
00:47:17,700 --> 00:47:20,467
But don't make any mistake.

1399
00:47:20,500 --> 00:47:23,767
I'm not saying anything wrong
about our chimpanzee brethren,

1400
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:25,633
only that I wish--
here's wishing

1401
00:47:25,667 --> 00:47:28,267
they'd throw a little more
work our way, all right?

1402
00:47:28,300 --> 00:47:32,533
-Lemur, the lemur--
L-E-M-U-R. Hey.

1403
00:47:32,567 --> 00:47:34,367
-Hey, who's this bird-dog thing?

1404
00:47:34,433 --> 00:47:36,667
I don't like him.

1405
00:47:36,700 --> 00:47:39,500
-L is for lemur--

1406
00:47:39,533 --> 00:47:40,800
-L is for lemur.

1407
00:47:40,833 --> 00:47:42,200
Enough said.

1408
00:47:42,233 --> 00:47:43,667
-E is for eat.

1409
00:47:43,700 --> 00:47:44,767
-E is for eat.

1410
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:47,467
I eat four times my own
weight in nuts and berries,

1411
00:47:47,500 --> 00:47:50,767
which has its consequences,
but go figure.

1412
00:47:50,800 --> 00:47:52,733
-M is for monkey.

1413
00:47:52,767 --> 00:47:53,433
-Monkey.

1414
00:47:53,467 --> 00:47:55,200
I'm often mistaken for a monkey.

1415
00:47:55,233 --> 00:47:56,733
It goes with the turf.

1416
00:47:56,767 --> 00:47:57,233
Let's go.

1417
00:47:57,267 --> 00:47:58,833
-U is for unusual.

1418
00:47:58,867 --> 00:48:00,633
-And unpredictable.

1419
00:48:00,667 --> 00:48:02,267
-Unpredictable is right.

1420
00:48:02,300 --> 00:48:04,733
I once took a whiz on
Johnny Carson's sport coat.

1421
00:48:04,767 --> 00:48:06,000
I don't panel well.

1422
00:48:06,033 --> 00:48:07,733
OK, on with the show.

1423
00:48:07,733 --> 00:48:08,733
-R is for radical.

1424
00:48:08,767 --> 00:48:09,733
-And rambunctious.

1425
00:48:09,767 --> 00:48:12,467
-Randy as a jackrabbit,
that's me, all right.

1426
00:48:12,500 --> 00:48:13,367
Woo.

1427
00:48:13,400 --> 00:48:14,967
-I guess it's the
splendiferous lemur.

1428
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:16,967
-Friend to all mankind.

1429
00:48:17,000 --> 00:48:20,767
-Please consider me as a
possible corporate symbol

1430
00:48:20,800 --> 00:48:24,367
or mascot, suitable and
fine for any professional

1431
00:48:24,400 --> 00:48:26,367
or semi-professional sport team.

1432
00:48:26,400 --> 00:48:27,700
-It's the splendiferous--

1433
00:48:27,733 --> 00:48:28,533
--magnificent--

1434
00:48:28,567 --> 00:48:29,433
--lemur!

1435
00:48:29,467 --> 00:48:32,833
-I, the lemur, beg
you to consider me.

1436
00:48:32,867 --> 00:48:34,800
I will-- I'm willing
to travel and would

1437
00:48:34,833 --> 00:48:39,800
make an excellent companion
to any elderly or unelderly

1438
00:48:39,833 --> 00:48:40,500
person.

1439
00:48:40,533 --> 00:48:42,733
Gentlemen, please consider me.

1440
00:48:42,767 --> 00:48:43,733
Thank you.

1441
00:48:43,767 --> 00:48:44,400
Won't you--

1442
00:48:44,433 --> 00:48:45,733
[buzzing]

1443
00:48:45,767 --> 00:48:46,333
-Movie sign!

1444
00:48:46,367 --> 00:48:46,767
-Whoa.

1445
00:48:57,633 --> 00:48:59,667
-Get off-- get him
off of me, Joel.

1446
00:48:59,700 --> 00:49:00,433
-Hey, Servo.

1447
00:49:00,467 --> 00:49:01,033
Fight back.

1448
00:49:01,067 --> 00:49:01,833
-I can't.

1449
00:49:01,867 --> 00:49:03,067
Get that little thing--

1450
00:49:03,100 --> 00:49:04,400
-Hey, get that
monkey away from me.

1451
00:49:04,433 --> 00:49:05,100
-What is that anyway?

1452
00:49:05,133 --> 00:49:05,933
-It's a lemur.

1453
00:49:05,967 --> 00:49:07,133
They said in the
film guide that he's

1454
00:49:07,167 --> 00:49:09,433
going to be in-- we're gonna
meet him later in the film.

1455
00:49:09,467 --> 00:49:09,867
-Get rid of him.

1456
00:49:09,900 --> 00:49:11,000
Thank you.

1457
00:49:11,033 --> 00:49:11,533
-Oh, I'm dead.

1458
00:49:11,567 --> 00:49:14,533
-Hold that thought.

1459
00:49:14,567 --> 00:49:16,000
-Hi, remember me?

1460
00:49:16,033 --> 00:49:17,233
I'm Satan.

1461
00:49:17,267 --> 00:49:19,433
This is the first part of my
three picture development deal.

1462
00:49:19,467 --> 00:49:21,933
We'll be right back.

1463
00:49:21,967 --> 00:49:24,400
Now here I go down her back.

1464
00:49:24,433 --> 00:49:25,367
Watch this.

1465
00:49:25,400 --> 00:49:26,867
It's a hoot.

1466
00:49:26,900 --> 00:49:29,400
[Gibberish]

1467
00:49:29,433 --> 00:49:31,133
[Screaming]

1468
00:49:31,167 --> 00:49:32,133
[Gunfire]

1469
00:49:32,167 --> 00:49:34,500
-Shoot the snake, not the girl.

1470
00:49:34,533 --> 00:49:35,100
[Sobbing]

1471
00:49:35,133 --> 00:49:36,900
-On second thought.

1472
00:49:36,933 --> 00:49:38,800
-Oh, well, that does it.

1473
00:49:38,833 --> 00:49:40,867
-Oh, let's get out
of this scary planet.

1474
00:49:40,900 --> 00:49:42,400
-What do you say we
fix ourselves a place

1475
00:49:42,433 --> 00:49:43,567
and sleep here?

1476
00:49:43,600 --> 00:49:45,733
It'll be a lot easier to
find our way in the daylight.

1477
00:49:45,767 --> 00:49:49,033
-Isn't it daylight now?

1478
00:49:49,067 --> 00:49:50,633
-Hm.

1479
00:49:50,667 --> 00:49:52,667
-They all have cataracts.

1480
00:49:52,700 --> 00:49:54,667
-Oh, I understand.

1481
00:49:54,700 --> 00:49:57,067
-Maybe it's the planet
of the midnight sun.

1482
00:49:57,100 --> 00:49:59,033
-And so they chop
and slice and dice.

1483
00:49:59,067 --> 00:50:02,500
And of course, they install
beautiful Anderson windows.

1484
00:50:02,533 --> 00:50:05,500
America-- know-how at its best.

1485
00:50:05,533 --> 00:50:07,933
-And the women. helped
in gathering up things

1486
00:50:07,967 --> 00:50:08,967
and put it against the lean to.

1487
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:12,467
-Saggy roots and
nuts and diapers.

1488
00:50:12,500 --> 00:50:13,733
-Uh, why didn't use
the tent that they

1489
00:50:13,767 --> 00:50:14,800
had in their backpacks?

1490
00:50:14,833 --> 00:50:15,900
-Uh, they're artists.

1491
00:50:15,933 --> 00:50:16,500
-Oh.

1492
00:50:16,533 --> 00:50:16,933
-Yeah.

1493
00:50:21,067 --> 00:50:23,067
-Hey, how about that?

1494
00:50:23,100 --> 00:50:23,500
Home sweet home.

1495
00:50:23,533 --> 00:50:24,000
-It's beautiful.

1496
00:50:24,033 --> 00:50:25,567
-What a sweet job.

1497
00:50:25,600 --> 00:50:27,100
-Let's go to the front
desk and register.

1498
00:50:27,133 --> 00:50:28,167
[Hooting]

1499
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:29,667
-Oh, a horny old owl.

1500
00:50:29,700 --> 00:50:30,567
-That's an owl.

1501
00:50:30,600 --> 00:50:31,533
-The own footage is
not what it seems.

1502
00:50:34,300 --> 00:50:35,867
-It's going to be
real comfortable.

1503
00:50:35,900 --> 00:50:37,767
-Well, it's not the
Waldorf, but I like it.

1504
00:50:37,800 --> 00:50:40,967
-It is the Waldorf
salad, though.

1505
00:50:41,000 --> 00:50:43,600
-Well, let's get the packs.

1506
00:50:43,633 --> 00:50:44,900
Now, Ralph and I
are going to split

1507
00:50:44,933 --> 00:50:47,000
the watches, three hours apiece.

1508
00:50:47,033 --> 00:50:48,967
That should take us
up until daylight.

1509
00:50:49,000 --> 00:50:50,267
You girls get some sleep.

1510
00:50:50,300 --> 00:50:52,167
-No reason why we
can't take a watch too.

1511
00:50:52,200 --> 00:50:53,133
-Yes, there is.

1512
00:50:53,167 --> 00:50:53,967
-How dare you?

1513
00:50:54,033 --> 00:50:54,633
-No arguments.

1514
00:50:54,667 --> 00:50:55,267
-You're girls.

1515
00:50:55,333 --> 00:50:56,933
-Now get some sleep.

1516
00:50:56,967 --> 00:50:58,133
Ralph, I'll take the first one.

1517
00:50:58,167 --> 00:50:59,033
-Ok.

1518
00:50:59,067 --> 00:51:00,367
Wake me up a little
earlier, will you?

1519
00:51:00,400 --> 00:51:01,000
-Dames.

1520
00:51:04,700 --> 00:51:05,100
-Well.

1521
00:51:09,967 --> 00:51:13,067
-Boy, you burn a human body,
there's not much left of him.

1522
00:51:13,100 --> 00:51:14,300
Oh, there's his ring.

1523
00:51:14,333 --> 00:51:15,267
-A couple of molars.

1524
00:51:15,300 --> 00:51:17,867
They don't burn.

1525
00:51:17,900 --> 00:51:19,800
[Imitating soundtrack]

1526
00:51:24,367 --> 00:51:27,067
-Huh, bookends.

1527
00:51:27,100 --> 00:51:29,233
-And he's the librarian.

1528
00:51:29,267 --> 00:51:29,867
Yo.

1529
00:51:34,833 --> 00:51:36,200
-Come on, you bastards.

1530
00:51:36,233 --> 00:51:39,933
I'm ready for you.

1531
00:51:39,967 --> 00:51:40,967
-Hi, God.

1532
00:51:44,367 --> 00:51:45,200
-Hey.

1533
00:51:45,233 --> 00:51:46,867
I thought you were
going to call me.

1534
00:51:46,900 --> 00:51:47,900
-I'm OK.

1535
00:51:47,933 --> 00:51:48,800
-You're OK.

1536
00:51:48,833 --> 00:51:50,000
-Thought as long as
I felt all right,

1537
00:51:50,033 --> 00:51:51,667
I'd stay with it a while longer.

1538
00:51:51,700 --> 00:51:55,067
-Hey, your microphone
cord is showing.

1539
00:51:55,100 --> 00:51:55,967
-Good night, old man.

1540
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:56,867
-I'm 35.

1541
00:51:56,900 --> 00:51:57,300
I'm not old.

1542
00:51:57,333 --> 00:51:58,300
Get out of here.

1543
00:51:58,333 --> 00:51:59,833
I could still take you, buddy.

1544
00:52:04,533 --> 00:52:05,833
-Come on, you bastards.

1545
00:52:05,867 --> 00:52:08,267
Come at me.

1546
00:52:08,300 --> 00:52:10,800
-Hm, nothing.

1547
00:52:10,833 --> 00:52:13,300
Just little animals.

1548
00:52:13,333 --> 00:52:15,233
[Imitating soundtrack]

1549
00:52:18,100 --> 00:52:19,200
-Oh.

1550
00:52:19,233 --> 00:52:20,400
Oh.

1551
00:52:20,433 --> 00:52:22,233
Oh, where's my man?

1552
00:52:22,267 --> 00:52:24,767
Well, you're not--
you're not my man.

1553
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:28,133
My man must be outside.

1554
00:52:28,167 --> 00:52:29,100
I know you're not him.

1555
00:52:29,133 --> 00:52:30,833
-Ooh, is that my stomach.

1556
00:52:30,867 --> 00:52:32,033
I better--

1557
00:52:32,067 --> 00:52:34,233
-Penny for your thoughts.

1558
00:52:34,233 --> 00:52:36,433
-I love the culottes.

1559
00:52:36,467 --> 00:52:38,833
-Can't you sleep?

1560
00:52:38,867 --> 00:52:40,300
-I need a glass of water.

1561
00:52:43,833 --> 00:52:44,767
-I don't know.

1562
00:52:44,800 --> 00:52:47,133
It's-- . it's just that--

1563
00:52:47,167 --> 00:52:48,433
-I don't know.

1564
00:52:48,467 --> 00:52:50,867
--that I feel so much--

1565
00:52:50,900 --> 00:52:51,867
[muffled]

1566
00:52:55,967 --> 00:52:57,100
-You got my tongue.

1567
00:52:57,133 --> 00:52:59,533
-They both awake with the
worst breath of the morning.

1568
00:52:59,567 --> 00:53:01,167
-Tell me, doctor, do you
still want to marry me?

1569
00:53:01,200 --> 00:53:02,000
-Ha.

1570
00:53:02,033 --> 00:53:03,367
I wouldn't marry
you if you were one

1571
00:53:03,400 --> 00:53:04,967
of three people on this planet.

1572
00:53:08,333 --> 00:53:08,933
-Clink.

1573
00:53:11,533 --> 00:53:14,133
-Should we wake the others?

1574
00:53:14,167 --> 00:53:16,867
-I don't think so.

1575
00:53:16,900 --> 00:53:17,300
-Ok.

1576
00:53:20,267 --> 00:53:22,467
-Do you like long
walks in the rain?

1577
00:53:22,500 --> 00:53:24,000
Chinese food?

1578
00:53:24,033 --> 00:53:26,233
Mushing up your ice cream?

1579
00:53:26,267 --> 00:53:30,333
Those little Necco wafers that
they used to-- oh, never mind.

1580
00:53:30,367 --> 00:53:31,333
Love me.

1581
00:53:31,367 --> 00:53:32,233
-I'm watching over you now.

1582
00:53:32,267 --> 00:53:32,867
Procreate.

1583
00:53:41,533 --> 00:53:44,533
-Hi, I couldn't help noticing
your suitcase and your shoes.

1584
00:53:49,067 --> 00:53:51,033
-Hum de do, do do-- ho!

1585
00:53:55,967 --> 00:53:57,333
[Screaming]

1586
00:53:57,367 --> 00:53:58,700
-Hurts, don't it?

1587
00:53:58,733 --> 00:54:00,367
-Good scream.

1588
00:54:00,400 --> 00:54:02,433
-Sounds like an
alligator mauling Bob.

1589
00:54:06,300 --> 00:54:07,067
-Yeah, that hurt.

1590
00:54:07,100 --> 00:54:07,700
-He's got him now.

1591
00:54:07,733 --> 00:54:10,100
I can't believe it, Wally.

1592
00:54:10,133 --> 00:54:11,567
There's a foreign
object in the ring.

1593
00:54:11,600 --> 00:54:13,167
he's gonna do--
oh, a pile driver.

1594
00:54:13,200 --> 00:54:13,567
Oh no.

1595
00:54:13,600 --> 00:54:14,800
-Oh, no.

1596
00:54:14,833 --> 00:54:16,967
If you rub my belly-- my nerve
endings are all down there.

1597
00:54:17,000 --> 00:54:19,333
-Oh, gotcha.

1598
00:54:19,367 --> 00:54:21,700
-It looks like Dr. Moto's
got a strangle hold on him.

1599
00:54:25,033 --> 00:54:26,067
-Oh.

1600
00:54:26,100 --> 00:54:29,000
-That's not fair.

1601
00:54:29,033 --> 00:54:31,700
-Oh, he used a foreign
object all right.

1602
00:54:31,733 --> 00:54:35,533
-I was wondering if we could
finish our walk la-- later.

1603
00:54:35,567 --> 00:54:37,733
-He's down.

1604
00:54:37,767 --> 00:54:38,700
-Oh, Ralph.

1605
00:54:38,733 --> 00:54:39,233
Ralph, Ralph.

1606
00:54:39,267 --> 00:54:39,767
-Get out of the way.

1607
00:54:39,800 --> 00:54:41,267
You had your chance.

1608
00:54:41,300 --> 00:54:42,233
-Let's get him back to camp.

1609
00:54:42,267 --> 00:54:43,033
-Ralph is ralphing.

1610
00:54:43,067 --> 00:54:44,100
Look at that.

1611
00:54:44,133 --> 00:54:44,667
Oh, yuck.

1612
00:54:47,633 --> 00:54:49,267
Good job, Blondie.

1613
00:54:52,067 --> 00:54:53,800
-Everyone, Ralph's dead.

1614
00:54:53,833 --> 00:54:55,600
-They are everyone.

1615
00:54:55,633 --> 00:54:57,767
-Oh.

1616
00:54:57,800 --> 00:54:59,600
Here just set him
here on this body bag.

1617
00:54:59,633 --> 00:55:01,467
-I can't find a kit.

1618
00:55:01,500 --> 00:55:04,267
-And smiling.

1619
00:55:04,300 --> 00:55:06,800
-Get the kit.

1620
00:55:06,833 --> 00:55:08,667
Get me the canteen.

1621
00:55:08,700 --> 00:55:09,300
Get the canteen.

1622
00:55:09,333 --> 00:55:11,767
-Oh, Harrisman on the job.

1623
00:55:11,800 --> 00:55:13,667
-I swear to god.

1624
00:55:13,700 --> 00:55:15,400
Gotta do everything
my sorry self.

1625
00:55:15,433 --> 00:55:18,133
-Nora.

1626
00:55:18,167 --> 00:55:18,667
-No, you idiot.

1627
00:55:18,700 --> 00:55:20,167
That's my saxophone.

1628
00:55:20,200 --> 00:55:22,333
-Get that rag wet.

1629
00:55:22,367 --> 00:55:23,733
[Sobbing]

1630
00:55:23,767 --> 00:55:27,533
-Aw, looks like he
lost a pie contest.

1631
00:55:27,567 --> 00:55:29,500
-Oh, it's all my fault.

1632
00:55:29,533 --> 00:55:30,667
-Bingo!

1633
00:55:30,700 --> 00:55:32,567
-It's nobody's fault.

1634
00:55:32,600 --> 00:55:34,700
-He's a chocolate mess.

1635
00:55:34,733 --> 00:55:36,533
-You know you're not
supposed to leave camp.

1636
00:55:36,567 --> 00:55:39,133
-Hey, you're spending a lot of
time on that one nipple there.

1637
00:55:39,167 --> 00:55:39,767
You want that around?

1638
00:55:42,500 --> 00:55:44,533
-We've got to keep a
sharp lookout from now on.

1639
00:55:47,767 --> 00:55:51,633
[Painful screaming]

1640
00:55:51,667 --> 00:55:54,833
-Boy, I feel like I wrestled
an alligator last night.

1641
00:55:54,867 --> 00:55:55,633
-Hey, what do you know?

1642
00:55:55,667 --> 00:55:58,367
I'm all right, and
now she's dead.

1643
00:56:02,900 --> 00:56:04,000
-Uh-oh, breakfast time.

1644
00:56:04,033 --> 00:56:05,433
Honey Nut Cheerios, guys.

1645
00:56:05,467 --> 00:56:06,433
-Hahaha.

1646
00:56:06,467 --> 00:56:10,233
A heaping bowl.

1647
00:56:10,267 --> 00:56:11,967
-I'm going to need
a bigger shoe.

1648
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:13,467
We're going to get a
bigger shoe, right?

1649
00:56:16,500 --> 00:56:17,667
-Yeah, yeah.

1650
00:56:17,700 --> 00:56:19,200
I'm dealing with it.

1651
00:56:19,233 --> 00:56:19,967
I got it.

1652
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:21,567
I-- I got it, honey.

1653
00:56:21,600 --> 00:56:23,800
[Gunfire]

1654
00:56:23,833 --> 00:56:25,733
-It sounds like it
swallowed a dolphin.

1655
00:56:25,767 --> 00:56:28,367
-No.

1656
00:56:28,433 --> 00:56:30,567
Oh Ralph, no!

1657
00:56:30,600 --> 00:56:31,067
-Oh.

1658
00:56:31,100 --> 00:56:33,333
Need a bigger gun.

1659
00:56:33,367 --> 00:56:35,000
Whoa.

1660
00:56:35,033 --> 00:56:36,167
-He solarized him.

1661
00:56:36,200 --> 00:56:39,967
-I haven't seen a wasp that
big since the Nixon years.

1662
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:41,467
-Nyuk, nyuk, nyuk.

1663
00:56:41,500 --> 00:56:42,900
That would be a [INAUDIBLE].

1664
00:56:42,933 --> 00:56:44,400
-Mm-hmm.

1665
00:56:44,433 --> 00:56:45,033
-Help me!

1666
00:56:45,067 --> 00:56:48,333
Help me!

1667
00:56:48,367 --> 00:56:50,367
-Where is everybody?

1668
00:56:50,400 --> 00:56:52,700
-Oh, they've gone.

1669
00:56:52,733 --> 00:56:56,533
They've gone back to the ship
for supplies and equipment.

1670
00:56:56,567 --> 00:56:59,800
You've been unconscious
for a day and a half.

1671
00:56:59,833 --> 00:57:02,333
-Oh, I don't remember
what happened.

1672
00:57:02,367 --> 00:57:05,733
-You were hurt, but
you're all right now.

1673
00:57:05,767 --> 00:57:08,433
-Help me, help me.

1674
00:57:08,467 --> 00:57:09,867
-You've been here all alone?

1675
00:57:09,900 --> 00:57:11,000
-80-foot bugs give
me the creeps.

1676
00:57:11,033 --> 00:57:12,900
-Somebody had to stay with you.

1677
00:57:12,933 --> 00:57:15,567
You couldn't be left alone.

1678
00:57:15,600 --> 00:57:17,367
-Well, I'm all right now.

1679
00:57:17,400 --> 00:57:18,733
-Is he OK?

1680
00:57:18,767 --> 00:57:20,067
-Nah.

1681
00:57:20,100 --> 00:57:22,067
-I've got a headache
this big, and it's

1682
00:57:22,100 --> 00:57:24,067
got stock footage
written all over it.

1683
00:57:24,100 --> 00:57:26,400
-You've got to relax and rest.

1684
00:57:26,433 --> 00:57:27,400
-Relax?

1685
00:57:27,433 --> 00:57:28,600
There's a bee the size
of a moose over there,

1686
00:57:28,633 --> 00:57:30,500
and you want him to relax?

1687
00:57:30,533 --> 00:57:33,067
-Come here.

1688
00:57:33,100 --> 00:57:34,933
I need some medicine.

1689
00:57:34,933 --> 00:57:36,800
-Daddy needs his love medicine.

1690
00:57:42,067 --> 00:57:44,000
We shouldn't be watching this.

1691
00:57:44,033 --> 00:57:45,867
-When will they be back?

1692
00:57:45,900 --> 00:57:46,833
-Real soon.

1693
00:57:46,867 --> 00:57:48,767
Try to rest.

1694
00:57:48,800 --> 00:57:52,067
-Tell the bee I love him.

1695
00:57:52,100 --> 00:57:53,700
-Oh, now he's dead again.

1696
00:57:56,600 --> 00:57:59,567
-Oh, son of a rotten--
--stupid alligator

1697
00:57:59,600 --> 00:58:07,433
pushing [MUTTERING]
Hey, let's carry

1698
00:58:07,467 --> 00:58:09,467
all this crap around the rock.

1699
00:58:09,500 --> 00:58:12,100
-Kill it! kill it!

1700
00:58:12,133 --> 00:58:13,900
-Is that your
little friend, Joel?

1701
00:58:13,933 --> 00:58:14,600
-Yeah.

1702
00:58:14,633 --> 00:58:15,933
I guess that's the lemur, yeah.

1703
00:58:15,967 --> 00:58:17,067
-Hey, where'd you
pick this one up?

1704
00:58:17,100 --> 00:58:18,867
-He jumped right
out of Paul's chest.

1705
00:58:18,900 --> 00:58:20,467
-That's Joe.

1706
00:58:20,500 --> 00:58:21,133
-Hello, Joe.

1707
00:58:21,167 --> 00:58:21,967
What do you know?

1708
00:58:22,000 --> 00:58:22,767
-Hey, Joe.

1709
00:58:22,800 --> 00:58:23,767
Go investigate the lady.

1710
00:58:23,800 --> 00:58:24,967
Wake her up, boy.

1711
00:58:25,000 --> 00:58:25,400
-Hey.

1712
00:58:25,433 --> 00:58:27,500
-He's hungry.

1713
00:58:27,533 --> 00:58:28,800
-Oh, hi.

1714
00:58:28,833 --> 00:58:30,833
Boy am I glad you're back.

1715
00:58:30,867 --> 00:58:32,867
Did you have a good trip?

1716
00:58:32,900 --> 00:58:35,900
-Lovely if you like walking.

1717
00:58:35,933 --> 00:58:37,900
-Anything usual, Dick?

1718
00:58:37,933 --> 00:58:39,233
[Laughter]

1719
00:58:39,267 --> 00:58:40,900
-What's unusual anymore?

1720
00:58:40,933 --> 00:58:42,833
I saw something that
looked like a Sherman tank,

1721
00:58:42,867 --> 00:58:44,700
but it didn't bother us.

1722
00:58:44,733 --> 00:58:46,233
-Hey, who's the cook
in the outfit tonight?

1723
00:58:46,267 --> 00:58:47,567
-I'll do it.

1724
00:58:47,600 --> 00:58:48,233
-Yeah.

1725
00:58:48,267 --> 00:58:49,900
How do you like your lemur?

1726
00:58:49,933 --> 00:58:51,900
-This one's been
eating all day long.

1727
00:58:51,933 --> 00:58:52,567
-Hm, this one.

1728
00:58:52,600 --> 00:58:53,567
-Good.

1729
00:58:53,600 --> 00:58:56,833
He'll get his strength
back faster that way.

1730
00:58:56,867 --> 00:59:01,300
-So we'll just, uh, let
this scene trail off, then.

1731
00:59:01,333 --> 00:59:02,933
-Hm, I don't know
about this lemur.

1732
00:59:02,967 --> 00:59:04,200
It tastes kind of gamy.

1733
00:59:04,233 --> 00:59:05,367
-And a little stringy.

1734
00:59:05,400 --> 00:59:06,633
-Yeah.

1735
00:59:06,667 --> 00:59:07,867
-They ate the lemur.

1736
00:59:07,900 --> 00:59:09,233
-Did you find
anything today, Dick?

1737
00:59:09,267 --> 00:59:10,967
Besides Joe, I mean.

1738
00:59:11,000 --> 00:59:12,767
-We got a whole bag
full of specimens.

1739
00:59:12,800 --> 00:59:13,733
-Ugh.

1740
00:59:13,767 --> 00:59:14,667
-Oh!

1741
00:59:14,700 --> 00:59:16,733
--this place will
support a lot of people.

1742
00:59:16,767 --> 00:59:18,767
If we had to stay here
for any length of time,

1743
00:59:18,800 --> 00:59:21,233
we should be able to live off
the land without much help.

1744
00:59:21,267 --> 00:59:22,600
-Ew, she's eating shoe polish.

1745
00:59:22,633 --> 00:59:24,333
-Thanks, but I'll
take you to USA.

1746
00:59:24,367 --> 00:59:26,267
-Me too.

1747
00:59:26,300 --> 00:59:28,033
-Hey, what are the
plans for tomorrow?

1748
00:59:28,067 --> 00:59:29,033
-Oh, I thought I'd
go to the mall.

1749
00:59:29,067 --> 00:59:30,867
Well, I thought Laura
and I'd finish our tests

1750
00:59:30,900 --> 00:59:31,867
and samplings, and then I--

1751
00:59:31,900 --> 00:59:34,000
-And then I want to take
a look at that island.

1752
00:59:34,033 --> 00:59:36,000
-All right, all right, we'll
go to your damn, dirty island.

1753
00:59:36,033 --> 00:59:37,167
-I seem to remember
some instructions

1754
00:59:37,200 --> 00:59:39,200
about not separating.

1755
00:59:39,233 --> 00:59:41,267
-We haven't run into anything
we can't handle, Ralph.

1756
00:59:41,300 --> 00:59:43,833
-You know, I think they all
read too much science fiction.

1757
00:59:43,867 --> 00:59:44,900
You know, they
probably thought we'd

1758
00:59:44,933 --> 00:59:47,100
meet some kind of super
race up here or something.

1759
00:59:47,133 --> 00:59:49,167
-And all we've met are
large, mutated animals.

1760
00:59:49,233 --> 00:59:50,867
-Why don't we all go together?

1761
00:59:50,900 --> 00:59:51,833
-That bee was pretty super-race.

1762
00:59:51,867 --> 00:59:54,233
-Doctor, you know better
than the rest of us

1763
00:59:54,267 --> 00:59:56,133
that you're in no
shape to travel.

1764
00:59:56,167 --> 00:59:56,900
-That's right.

1765
00:59:56,933 --> 00:59:58,100
-Where is he?

1766
00:59:58,133 --> 00:59:59,400
-So Nora and I will take one
of the rubber rafts tomorrow

1767
00:59:59,433 --> 01:00:01,167
and spend the day on the island.

1768
01:00:01,200 --> 01:00:04,700
Pat, you-- you do whatever
work you can around here.

1769
01:00:04,733 --> 01:00:06,333
-Yeah, why don't you stay
here and practice screaming.

1770
01:00:06,367 --> 01:00:07,300
[Roaring]

1771
01:00:07,333 --> 01:00:08,933
-Good, but back of the throat.

1772
01:00:08,967 --> 01:00:09,700
A little higher.

1773
01:00:12,167 --> 01:00:13,167
-Hi, remember me?

1774
01:00:13,200 --> 01:00:14,100
I'm Satan.

1775
01:00:14,133 --> 01:00:15,067
You never know where
I'm going to pop up.

1776
01:00:15,100 --> 01:00:17,233
But first, a recipe
from my pal, Ed Herlihy.

1777
01:00:20,167 --> 01:00:21,133
-[Inaudible].

1778
01:00:21,167 --> 01:00:22,900
-What are we going to do
about watches tonight?

1779
01:00:22,933 --> 01:00:23,833
-I'll take the first one.

1780
01:00:23,867 --> 01:00:24,867
I'll get some sleep
when it gets light.

1781
01:00:24,900 --> 01:00:27,233
-Hey, I heard that
business about the watches.

1782
01:00:27,267 --> 01:00:30,000
I may be a little weak, but
I can still handle a gun.

1783
01:00:30,033 --> 01:00:31,033
-Oh, don't be silly, Ralph.

1784
01:00:31,067 --> 01:00:32,333
You need your rest.

1785
01:00:32,367 --> 01:00:33,933
Look, maybe we
don't need a watch.

1786
01:00:33,967 --> 01:00:36,033
Joe seems to be pretty
good at shouting alarms.

1787
01:00:36,067 --> 01:00:37,833
-Count on Joe for extras.

1788
01:00:37,867 --> 01:00:40,867
-Oh, we can't afford
extras in this film.

1789
01:00:40,900 --> 01:00:46,167
So, we'll just, uh, drizzle
out of this scene too, huh?

1790
01:00:46,200 --> 01:00:48,100
[Hooting]

1791
01:00:48,133 --> 01:00:53,800
-Who-- who-- who could believe
that this film was made?

1792
01:00:53,833 --> 01:00:55,267
-A normal sized owl.

1793
01:00:55,333 --> 01:00:56,267
Who would have thought it?

1794
01:00:56,333 --> 01:00:59,200
-Yeah, crummy little--
I have to sit up here.

1795
01:00:59,233 --> 01:01:02,833
Where the hell'd
the bee go anyway?

1796
01:01:02,867 --> 01:01:03,567
-It "bee" gone.

1797
01:01:06,233 --> 01:01:10,267
-I have to sit here,
don't even have my roid

1798
01:01:10,300 --> 01:01:11,800
cushion and anything.

1799
01:01:16,900 --> 01:01:18,167
-Heh, cute old lemur.

1800
01:01:18,200 --> 01:01:20,467
Hey, he's eating his pen.

1801
01:01:20,500 --> 01:01:22,000
-Ha, ha.

1802
01:01:22,033 --> 01:01:24,000
Kooky.

1803
01:01:24,033 --> 01:01:26,100
-Here, suck on a
little JD, buddy.

1804
01:01:26,133 --> 01:01:28,167
-Hi, I'm back.

1805
